To generate the assert statement for the comment `// @@@ the cloned list is equal to the original list`, we need to ensure that the cloned list has the same elements in the same order as the original list. We can achieve this by comparing the size of both lists and then checking that each element at a given index in the original list is equal to the element at the same index in the cloned list.

Here is the assert statement:

<code>assert this.size() == ((LinkedList<E>) \result).size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(((LinkedList<E>) \result).get(i));</code>

This assert statement checks:
1. The size of the original list is equal to the size of the cloned list.
2. For each index `i` from `0` to `this.size() - 1`, the element at index `i` in the original list is equal to the element at index `i` in the cloned list.--------------------<code>assert this.size() == ((LinkedList<E>) \result).size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(((LinkedList<E>) \result).get(i));</code>--------------------To generate the assert statement for the comment `// @@@ the cloned list is equal to the original list`, we need to compare the elements of the original list and the cloned list. Since the `LinkedList` class does not provide a direct method to check equality of two lists, we can infer that the cloned list should have the same size and the same elements in the same order as the original list.

We can use the `size()` method to compare the sizes and the `get(int index)` method to compare the elements at each index. The assert statement should ensure that for every index `i` from `0` to `size() - 1`, the element at index `i` in the original list is equal to the element at index `i` in the cloned list.

Here is the assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(((LinkedList<E>) \result).get(i));</code>

This assert statement checks that for every valid index `i` in the range `[0, size() - 1]`, the element at index `i` in the original list (`this`) is equal to the element at index `i` in the cloned list (`\result`). Note that we cast `\result` to `LinkedList<E>` because `\result` is of type `Object` and we need to call the `get(int index)` method on it.--------------------